+# Catalyst integration preview
+
+Created with the repository's `create-challenge` skill and scaffolding command.
+This is a read-focused Yukon challenge board, not a remote evaluation service.
+
+## Preview without a backend or model spend
+
+From the Yukon repository root, start the explicit read-only fixture API:
+
+```sh
+bun run scripts/catalyst-fixture-api.ts --port 8099
+```
+
+In a second terminal:
+
+```sh
+NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8099 \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_CATALYST_BENCHMARK_REF=ca7a1000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001 \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_LIVE_CHALLENGES=catalyst \
+bun run dev:challenges
+```
+
+Open http://localhost:3000/catalyst. Viewing budgets of `0.75` and `8` produce
+different harness orderings. Both native maximization and minimization metrics
+are included. `?as=turing` is Yukon's development-only ownership preview; it
+does not sign in or grant permissions.
+
+The fixture makes no model calls, accepts no submissions or credentials, and
+labels all measurements as synthetic. Test the board in Chrome with:
+
+```sh
+bun run scripts/verify-catalyst-board.ts
+```
+
+## Public result contract
+
+The trusted judge publishes its ordinary Yukon Pareto packet. Its
+`officialMetrics.catalyst` contains:
+
+```text
+schemaVersion: 1
+evidence: "platform-verified" | "fixture"
+evaluationId: unique Catalyst execution attempt ID
+sourceDigest: source archive SHA-256
+imageDigest: sha256:<image digest>
+problem: {id, version: SHA-256, title, metric: {name, unit, direction: "+" | "-"}}
+harness: {id, version: SHA-256, title}
+model: exact model configuration identity
+conditions: exact execution-policy identity
+observations: [{cost: cumulative normalized model USD, score: native metric}, ...]
+```
+
+Only accepted submissions with a completed, valid Pareto packet and measured
+scores enter the matrix. Notes, claimed scores, promotion status, and local
+self-reports do not establish eligibility. A failed execution without a packet
+is distinct from an invalid judgment.
+
+One problem per Yukon track preserves native units and scoring direction.
+The configured benchmark anchors its challenge group; the board loads the
+Pareto tracks of that group. Harness rows join by exact source version and digest.
+Problem revisions, models, conditions, and evidence classes remain separate.
+
+Each cell takes each independent attempt's best observed score within the
+viewing budget, then displays score and cost medians. These are summary
+statistics, not necessarily a single achieved point. The Pareto frontier is
+computed separately for each problem; ordering uses the selected problem.
+Trajectories retain individual observations and stop at their last point.
+Repeated API records with the same execution identity count once.
+
+## Launch prerequisites
+
+Register the actual Pareto benchmark/challenge and replace the provisional
+`eigenlabs/catalyst` CLI name and repository link in `index.tsx`. Set its stable
+UUID as `NEXT_PUBLIC_CATALYST_BENCHMARK_REF`. An unconfigured board intentionally
+shows no benchmark rather than selecting an unrelated challenge.
+
+Add `catalyst` to `NEXT_PUBLIC_LIVE_CHALLENGES` only when launch is intended.
+Public environment settings are inlined; rebuild after changing them. Configure
+the preview/production origin in Supabase's redirect allowlist before sign-in.
+The legal routes intentionally contain `[LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED]`; supply actual
+documents before launch.
+
+Remote source builds, Dungeness worker jobs, private LLM grants, workflow
+authentication, spending authorization, and official result generation remain
+separate backend work. Credentials must never be added to source, Docker builds,
+PRs, public workflow inputs, or result metrics.
+
+Yukon's current real solver-profile API discovers promoted submissions only.
+Pareto submissions are not promoted. Before launch, that API needs a separate
+compatibility change to include accepted, valid Pareto participation. The fixture
+illustrates the intended shared portfolio and branded preview; it does not
+implement that database/API change.
